> By saying "Yes. Or you can pass the qtl object and model formula to stepwiseqtl(), starting the multi-qtl model exploration there", do you mean start from the max number of qtl before eliminating any qtl/qtl interactions with fit qtl, or do you mean after eliminating all the possible qtl/qtl interactions after run the serial  fitqtl steps?

No, I mean you can use stepwiseqtl() to perform the backward deletion. If you provide the arguments 'qtl' and 'formula', they are used as the starting point for the algorithm (instead of the null model, of no QTL).

> By saying "genome-wide scan permutation threshold" , do you mean the permutation from scanone?
>  Even if there are multiple qtl/interactions below the threshold, I should only excluding the one with the lowest threshold (not all below the threshold) to run fitqtl again, it this correct?

Yes I mean permutation threshold from scanone. Though for interactions, I'd want to use scantwo permutations.
Use the permutation thresholds as a guide, rather than the pointless p-values. You my perhaps use a less stringent significance threshold, depending on your goals.

karl

